1
00:00:05,777 --> 00:00:07,378
Sorry, I have to go.

2
00:00:08,046 --> 00:00:09,280
You didn't used to be like this.

3
00:00:10,882 --> 00:00:13,151
You never helped me when I needed it.

4
00:00:16,654 --> 00:00:17,989
YU
13 MISSED CALLS

5
00:00:18,056 --> 00:00:19,324
YU

6
00:00:22,727 --> 00:00:24,262
Stop this, Sora.

7
00:00:26,898 --> 00:00:28,233
-What the hell, damn it!
-Sora!

8
00:00:31,035 --> 00:00:32,203
What are you doing?

9
00:00:34,139 --> 00:00:35,440
Shut up!

10
00:00:38,009 --> 00:00:40,845
-Sora.
-This is none of your business.

11
00:00:40,912 --> 00:00:41,746
Go away!

12
00:00:56,794 --> 00:00:57,695
Yu.

13
00:01:13,077 --> 00:01:13,912
MIDDLE SCHOOL GRADUATION PARTY

14
00:01:13,978 --> 00:01:16,147
Hey, where's Tatsuki?

15
00:01:16,714 --> 00:01:18,449
He rushed out in a panic.

16
00:01:18,516 --> 00:01:20,351
Did something happen?

17
00:01:21,052 --> 00:01:21,886
Not sure.

18
00:01:27,492 --> 00:01:29,060
-Hello?
<i>-Tatsuki?</i>

19
00:01:30,028 --> 00:01:30,962
What happened?

20
00:01:32,664 --> 00:01:33,631
Are you okay?

21
00:01:48,413 --> 00:01:49,480
Thanks for coming.

22
00:01:50,448 --> 00:01:51,549
No problem at all.

23
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:52,884
Please come in.

24
00:01:53,585 --> 00:01:55,019
Excuse me.

25
00:01:56,888 --> 00:01:57,989
Hello.

26
00:01:58,489 --> 00:02:01,593
This is Mr. Mikumo, the representative,
and my co-worker Ms. Shizuku.

27
00:02:04,562 --> 00:02:06,364
Sorry for coming all of a sudden.

28
00:02:07,599 --> 00:02:09,434
I heard about what happened.

29
00:02:10,268 --> 00:02:11,236
Are you okay?

30
00:02:13,404 --> 00:02:14,272
Yes.

31
00:02:15,173 --> 00:02:18,476
Would you like to consult
a specialist about this?

32
00:02:18,543 --> 00:02:19,677
No.

33
00:02:21,646 --> 00:02:23,348
In situations like this,

34
00:02:23,414 --> 00:02:25,817
it's advised to put some distance
between both parties.

35
00:02:27,018 --> 00:02:29,654
Would you like to come over
to Yukanai right now?

36
00:02:30,588 --> 00:02:31,422
What?

37
00:02:32,123 --> 00:02:33,691
But Sora is…

38
00:02:33,758 --> 00:02:37,595
We will stay here and be with Sora.

39
00:02:38,096 --> 00:02:39,163
Yes.

40
00:02:55,813 --> 00:02:57,649
YUKANAI

41
00:02:58,516 --> 00:02:59,584
Hey.

42
00:03:00,084 --> 00:03:00,918
Hello.

43
00:03:00,985 --> 00:03:03,087
Come in. Sorry for the mess.

44
00:03:03,655 --> 00:03:04,822
I'm Fujinaga.

45
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:06,391
I'm Ajicchan.

46
00:03:06,891 --> 00:03:09,160
I bet you guys are hungry.

47
00:03:09,227 --> 00:03:10,628
Want some sandwiches?

48
00:03:11,529 --> 00:03:12,397
Want some?

49
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:13,998
Please don't mind me.

50
00:03:15,266 --> 00:03:17,201
I have some <i>takoyaki</i> mix left.

51
00:03:17,268 --> 00:03:18,903
Let's have <i>takoyaki!</i>

52
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:22,006
Let me see if we have octopus.

53
00:03:23,174 --> 00:03:24,042
This way.

54
00:03:35,219 --> 00:03:36,287
How long has it been

55
00:03:38,122 --> 00:03:40,291
since Sora started becoming
physically violent

56
00:03:41,459 --> 00:03:42,560
like that?

57
00:03:46,431 --> 00:03:48,700
I think after the suicide attempt.

58
00:03:55,306 --> 00:03:57,075
I don't understand why

59
00:03:58,076 --> 00:03:59,744
he did something like that.

60
00:04:02,213 --> 00:04:03,214
I see.

61
00:04:04,682 --> 00:04:07,652
And after that,
he barely came out of his room anymore

62
00:04:08,419 --> 00:04:10,254
<i>and he got more and more irritable.</i>

63
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:15,193
I just didn't know what to do,

64
00:04:15,793 --> 00:04:17,495
and when I tried talking
he just yelled at me.

65
00:04:18,996 --> 00:04:20,798
Then he started lashing out at things.

66
00:04:21,899 --> 00:04:23,835
Stop. Stop it.

67
00:04:23,901 --> 00:04:26,871
-Stop it.
-Let go of me! Get away!

68
00:04:33,311 --> 00:04:34,645
<i>Ever since then,</i>

69
00:04:36,147 --> 00:04:38,316
whenever something
rubbed him the wrong way, he'd…

70
00:04:52,130 --> 00:04:54,132
I failed to notice what was happening.

71
00:04:57,802 --> 00:04:59,070
I'm sorry.

72
00:05:02,373 --> 00:05:04,175
I thought about confiding in you,

73
00:05:05,176 --> 00:05:06,310
<i>but the timing was never right.</i>

74
00:05:06,377 --> 00:05:08,146
SORRY, I CAN'T MAKE IT JUST YET

75
00:05:08,946 --> 00:05:10,681
<i>And you always seemed to be busy.</i>

76
00:05:11,416 --> 00:05:14,852
Plus, I had decided
to raise him on my own,

77
00:05:15,887 --> 00:05:17,321
so relying on anyone else

78
00:05:17,388 --> 00:05:20,057
felt like I'd be admitting my failure,
and I couldn't do that.

79
00:05:23,594 --> 00:05:24,662
But in the end…

80
00:05:25,663 --> 00:05:26,597
No.

81
00:05:28,733 --> 00:05:31,736
Ultimately, it's all my fault.

82
00:05:40,745 --> 00:05:42,480
What should we do?

83
00:05:48,519 --> 00:05:52,390
All right!
Here's Ajicchan's special <i>takoyaki.</i>

84
00:05:53,691 --> 00:05:55,827
You might not be
in the mood for it right now,

85
00:05:55,893 --> 00:05:56,727
but please enjoy.

86
00:05:58,996 --> 00:06:01,065
We have a sleeping bag for guests,
so please use it.

87
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,203
Stay the night. You can take a bath too.

88
00:06:06,404 --> 00:06:07,238
But…

89
00:06:07,305 --> 00:06:10,641
Professor and Shi-chan will handle things
back at your house.

90
00:06:11,375 --> 00:06:12,210
Okay?

91
00:06:13,778 --> 00:06:16,214
I'll leave you to take care of the rest.

92
00:06:16,981 --> 00:06:17,849
Okay.

93
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:20,218
Thank you.

94
00:06:27,391 --> 00:06:28,426
Okay.

95
00:06:28,493 --> 00:06:31,596
Apparently, we're free to use
whatever ingredients are in the fridge.

96
00:06:31,662 --> 00:06:32,497
Thanks.

97
00:06:32,997 --> 00:06:34,232
Can you get the plates out?

98
00:06:34,298 --> 00:06:35,132
Okay.

99
00:06:37,034 --> 00:06:40,538
I can only hope that it will be
to you and Sora's liking.

100
00:06:40,605 --> 00:06:42,874
-Do you cook often?
-Yes.

101
00:06:43,374 --> 00:06:44,475
I sure do.

102
00:06:44,542 --> 00:06:46,544
I only make simple things though.

103
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,683
I wonder if Ms. Yu ever consulted
with the police

104
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,652
or the local authorities?

105
00:06:57,355 --> 00:06:59,557
She was probably shouldering it
all on her own.

106
00:07:00,958 --> 00:07:01,792
I bet.

107
00:07:02,293 --> 00:07:05,162
Ms. Yu's safety is what matters most.

108
00:07:06,230 --> 00:07:08,299
They'll have to discuss
the best course of action.

109
00:07:08,866 --> 00:07:10,768
It won't be an easy task.

110
00:07:12,236 --> 00:07:14,972
It's ready.

111
00:07:15,039 --> 00:07:17,308
-Please taste it, Shi-chan.
-Okay.

112
00:07:21,746 --> 00:07:22,914
It's good.

113
00:07:30,821 --> 00:07:31,889
Sora.

114
00:07:32,456 --> 00:07:34,492
I work with your dad
at the alternative school.

115
00:07:34,559 --> 00:07:35,893
My name is Mikumo.

116
00:07:36,594 --> 00:07:37,929
Sorry for coming all of a sudden.

117
00:07:40,331 --> 00:07:43,501
Everyone, including Ms. Shizuku and I,

118
00:07:44,368 --> 00:07:45,870
are on your side.

119
00:07:46,971 --> 00:07:48,472
Please believe that.

120
00:07:50,942 --> 00:07:54,045
But can I just say one thing?

121
00:07:55,479 --> 00:07:59,383
No matter the circumstances,
violence is never right.

122
00:08:01,485 --> 00:08:03,554
Unless you stop being violent,

123
00:08:04,388 --> 00:08:07,191
your mom will never be able
to come back home.

124
00:08:08,626 --> 00:08:10,261
We wouldn't want that, would we?

125
00:08:14,231 --> 00:08:15,466
Anyway…

126
00:08:18,169 --> 00:08:21,405
Aren't you hungry?

127
00:08:22,607 --> 00:08:26,077
I made some fried rice.
I'll leave it outside the door.

128
00:08:45,262 --> 00:08:47,031
Wow.

129
00:08:48,265 --> 00:08:49,300
MATERNAL AND CHILD HEALTH HANDBOOK

130
00:08:51,869 --> 00:08:53,904
They look so happy.

131
00:08:54,472 --> 00:08:55,606
Look at those smiling faces.

132
00:08:56,574 --> 00:08:59,610
Mr. Tatsuki had black hair back then?

133
00:09:00,878 --> 00:09:02,013
Yeah.

134
00:09:02,079 --> 00:09:04,649
He dyed it to that milk tea color
after working at Yukanai.

135
00:09:05,383 --> 00:09:06,484
Milk tea, huh?

136
00:09:09,754 --> 00:09:10,955
Shi-chan…

137
00:09:11,522 --> 00:09:12,356
Yes?

138
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:16,293
I can handle the rest on my own,
so you can head home for today.

139
00:09:17,228 --> 00:09:18,496
But…

140
00:09:18,562 --> 00:09:21,165
While you're at it,
I'd like you to stop by Yukanai too.

141
00:09:23,434 --> 00:09:24,268
Okay.

142
00:09:28,272 --> 00:09:30,841
-Sorry for causing you trouble.
-It's okay.

143
00:09:31,575 --> 00:09:32,977
How's Sora doing?

144
00:09:33,044 --> 00:09:36,147
Professor is staying close to him,

145
00:09:36,213 --> 00:09:37,248
so please be rest assured.

146
00:09:38,115 --> 00:09:38,949
Okay.

147
00:09:39,016 --> 00:09:42,319
These are the photos of Sora,
and some of his artwork

148
00:09:42,386 --> 00:09:44,588
I contacted you about borrowing
a little while ago.

149
00:09:45,156 --> 00:09:46,123
Why did you bring these?

150
00:09:47,024 --> 00:09:48,693
Professor Mikumo

151
00:09:48,759 --> 00:09:50,928
wanted the two of you to see them.

152
00:09:50,995 --> 00:09:52,963
I really want Tatsuki and Ms. Yu

153
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:54,965
to give "sharing" a try with these.

154
00:09:55,466 --> 00:09:57,134
Sharing?

155
00:09:59,336 --> 00:10:02,373
As the two of them look back
on their shared memories together,

156
00:10:03,274 --> 00:10:05,676
something just might come into view.

157
00:10:11,816 --> 00:10:12,650
Okay.

158
00:10:13,451 --> 00:10:15,653
Then I'll be going now.

159
00:10:16,654 --> 00:10:17,655
Thank you.

160
00:10:28,432 --> 00:10:29,567
MATERNAL AND CHILD HEALTH HANDBOOK

161
00:10:29,633 --> 00:10:30,768
SORA

162
00:10:32,236 --> 00:10:33,938
He was so small.

163
00:10:35,172 --> 00:10:37,742
When we brought him home
for the first time,

164
00:10:38,409 --> 00:10:40,344
he was so tiny and fragile,

165
00:10:40,845 --> 00:10:43,314
I remember feeling anxious,
wondering if we'd be able

166
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:44,281
to raise him properly.

167
00:11:06,937 --> 00:11:08,973
Where was this?

168
00:11:10,641 --> 00:11:12,676
The open space at Hayama Zoo.

169
00:11:14,712 --> 00:11:16,881
We went because he said
he wanted to see giraffes,

170
00:11:16,947 --> 00:11:18,749
but it was bigger than he expected

171
00:11:18,816 --> 00:11:20,785
so he got scared
and kept bawling the whole time.

172
00:11:21,585 --> 00:11:23,087
I don't remember that…

173
00:11:35,566 --> 00:11:36,400
Remember this?

174
00:11:39,003 --> 00:11:41,505
Sorry, I don't remember…

175
00:11:44,175 --> 00:11:45,810
You've forgotten all the family outings?

176
00:11:48,012 --> 00:11:49,346
I wonder why.

177
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,216
You were so engrossed with work.

178
00:11:52,783 --> 00:11:54,785
You were rarely home
on the weekends either.

179
00:12:05,029 --> 00:12:07,164
I'm not in any of these pictures.

180
00:12:09,767 --> 00:12:12,203
Sora and I often went out,
just the two of us.

181
00:12:22,413 --> 00:12:23,280
Look at this.

182
00:12:25,983 --> 00:12:27,218
Sora

183
00:12:27,718 --> 00:12:30,855
wasn't good at putting his feelings
into words, but…

184
00:12:32,656 --> 00:12:34,158
When I look at his drawings,

185
00:12:35,359 --> 00:12:38,462
I feel like I can somehow grasp
what he was trying to say.

186
00:12:40,798 --> 00:12:41,699
Yeah.

187
00:12:53,544 --> 00:12:54,712
What's that?

188
00:12:55,913 --> 00:12:59,083
It's from when he stopped going to school
soon after entering middle school.

189
00:13:18,335 --> 00:13:19,169
Sora.

190
00:13:21,572 --> 00:13:22,539
Sora.

191
00:13:30,614 --> 00:13:32,283
<i>Back then,</i>

192
00:13:33,217 --> 00:13:36,387
I kept on telling myself
that it was all to help Sora,

193
00:13:38,022 --> 00:13:40,524
but I was ignoring his feelings,
and pushing him into a corner.

194
00:13:41,025 --> 00:13:42,126
Sora.

195
00:13:42,192 --> 00:13:44,295
Staying holed up like that
won't solve anything.

196
00:13:45,829 --> 00:13:47,564
-Come out here.
-No.

197
00:13:47,631 --> 00:13:49,066
Stop it.

198
00:13:50,734 --> 00:13:51,669
Sora!

199
00:13:53,871 --> 00:13:56,307
No wonder he can't forgive me.

200
00:14:04,415 --> 00:14:06,083
I never consulted with you,

201
00:14:07,418 --> 00:14:08,519
and acted selfishly.

202
00:14:13,157 --> 00:14:14,191
And yet,

203
00:14:16,527 --> 00:14:18,329
I left you alone to deal with it.

204
00:14:19,930 --> 00:14:21,532
I'm really sorry.

205
00:14:47,224 --> 00:14:48,559
You were still drawing this?

206
00:14:53,163 --> 00:14:56,433
Sora loved this beach.

207
00:15:15,519 --> 00:15:16,453
Do you…

208
00:15:19,056 --> 00:15:20,057
remember this?

209
00:15:25,696 --> 00:15:27,898
It's the seashell Sora found for me.

210
00:15:30,501 --> 00:15:32,302
Here, this is for you.

211
00:15:34,671 --> 00:15:35,706
-It's pretty.
-Right?

212
00:15:35,773 --> 00:15:36,874
Thanks.

213
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:38,308
Okay, Dad, let's race.

214
00:15:51,388 --> 00:15:52,956
You still have it?

215
00:16:04,068 --> 00:16:06,270
Where did things go wrong?

216
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:28,625
I'm worried about Sora,
so I'll go back home.

217
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:30,594
Should I go too?

218
00:16:31,795 --> 00:16:32,629
It's okay.

219
00:16:41,405 --> 00:16:42,806
Okay, got it.

220
00:16:50,013 --> 00:16:51,081
Good morning.

221
00:16:51,148 --> 00:16:52,616
Hold on, Sora.

222
00:16:55,285 --> 00:16:56,386
Who are you?

223
00:16:59,456 --> 00:17:01,825
I'm Mikumo,
the one who made that fried rice.

224
00:17:02,893 --> 00:17:04,261
Why are you still here?

225
00:17:04,761 --> 00:17:05,629
Sorry.

226
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:08,699
I was worried about leaving you all alone.

227
00:17:10,701 --> 00:17:12,803
-How annoying.
-Hey, Sora.

228
00:17:15,506 --> 00:17:18,108
Do you want to try going to Yukanai?

229
00:17:18,809 --> 00:17:19,676
What?

230
00:17:20,177 --> 00:17:21,011
He's there, right?

231
00:17:21,078 --> 00:17:23,046
Your dad? Yeah, he'll be there.

232
00:17:25,582 --> 00:17:26,583
I don't want to see him.

233
00:17:27,384 --> 00:17:28,385
I see.

234
00:17:30,721 --> 00:17:31,822
What are

235
00:17:32,990 --> 00:17:34,992
your feelings towards your dad right now?

236
00:17:38,795 --> 00:17:43,100
Is he annoying, infuriating,
or maybe you just don't care?

237
00:17:49,706 --> 00:17:50,641
I can't forgive him.

238
00:17:53,744 --> 00:17:55,112
That's understandable.

239
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,548
I'm sure you can't.

240
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:02,653
But I don't think
you need to hold back those feelings.

241
00:18:03,754 --> 00:18:07,224
At Yukanai, you’re free
to spend your time however you like.

242
00:18:08,959 --> 00:18:10,661
If you’re tired, you can just sleep.

243
00:18:12,763 --> 00:18:13,964
Why not come and check it out?

244
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:18,068
If you don't like it, you can leave.

245
00:18:19,269 --> 00:18:20,103
How does that sound?

246
00:18:25,909 --> 00:18:28,612
All right, it’s time for our annual
Yukanai festival!

247
00:18:28,679 --> 00:18:30,314
What kind of festival
would you like to have this year?

248
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:31,215
Yakisoba festival.

249
00:18:31,281 --> 00:18:32,416
Baseball tournament.

250
00:18:32,482 --> 00:18:33,850
I really want to play baseball.

251
00:18:33,917 --> 00:18:35,118
I want a giant paella.

252
00:18:35,185 --> 00:18:36,954
-Mochitsuki festival.
-Great Detective Saku.

253
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:38,322
Don't speak all at once.

254
00:18:38,388 --> 00:18:40,224
-Paella.
-I can't hear everyone at once.

255
00:18:40,290 --> 00:18:41,692
Mochitsuki festival.

256
00:18:41,758 --> 00:18:43,193
Mochitsuki sounds fun.

257
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:44,661
What do you want to do, Tatsuki?

258
00:18:47,297 --> 00:18:48,332
Let's see…

259
00:18:48,398 --> 00:18:50,367
Your energy is so low, Tatsuki.

260
00:18:50,434 --> 00:18:51,969
Yeah, let's get pumped up.

261
00:18:52,035 --> 00:18:53,003
Sorry, I spaced out.

262
00:18:54,871 --> 00:18:56,506
Great Detective Sakura.

263
00:19:01,578 --> 00:19:03,380
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

264
00:19:03,447 --> 00:19:05,349
How's Sora?

265
00:19:05,415 --> 00:19:06,917
He's in his room right now.

266
00:19:08,218 --> 00:19:09,886
I actually just asked Sora

267
00:19:09,953 --> 00:19:12,489
if he'd like to go to Yukanai with me.

268
00:19:13,423 --> 00:19:14,658
Would that be all right?

269
00:19:14,725 --> 00:19:16,593
-To Yukanai?
-Yes.

270
00:19:17,594 --> 00:19:19,863
I'm okay with it if he wants to go.

271
00:19:25,736 --> 00:19:27,537
All right, we'll be off.

272
00:19:28,138 --> 00:19:29,373
I'll contact you later.

273
00:19:30,741 --> 00:19:31,842
Okay.

274
00:19:31,908 --> 00:19:33,543
Please take this chance to rest.

275
00:19:33,610 --> 00:19:34,711
Bye.

276
00:19:35,612 --> 00:19:36,480
Let's go.

277
00:19:47,190 --> 00:19:49,259
Raise your hands for the paella.

278
00:19:49,326 --> 00:19:52,696
-Raise your hand.
-Raise your hand for the paella.

279
00:19:52,763 --> 00:19:55,532
-One, two, three…
-Everyone, raise your hand.

280
00:19:55,599 --> 00:19:56,900
Raise your hand.

281
00:19:56,967 --> 00:19:58,335
Seriously?

282
00:19:58,402 --> 00:20:00,003
Come inside.

283
00:20:05,008 --> 00:20:06,376
That's a lot of people.

284
00:20:06,443 --> 00:20:08,378
One, two, three, four, five…

285
00:20:22,192 --> 00:20:24,294
Who wants to vote for baseball?

286
00:20:24,361 --> 00:20:26,496
At Yukanai, we decide everything
through meetings.

287
00:20:26,563 --> 00:20:28,398
You can do whatever you want here.

288
00:20:28,465 --> 00:20:30,334
Paella!

289
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:33,036
Hide-and-seek.

290
00:20:35,439 --> 00:20:38,175
I thought it might be better
than being stuck at home.

291
00:20:49,319 --> 00:20:51,621
Hey Shi-chan. Who's that?

292
00:20:52,122 --> 00:20:53,757
Is that a new student?

293
00:20:53,824 --> 00:20:54,725
His name is Sora.

294
00:20:54,791 --> 00:20:56,059
Is he nervous?

295
00:20:57,861 --> 00:20:58,695
Maybe.

296
00:20:58,762 --> 00:21:01,131
-Okay, I'm going to talk to him.
-I'll go too.

297
00:21:01,198 --> 00:21:02,032
Me too.

298
00:21:02,099 --> 00:21:03,300
Let's go.

299
00:21:03,367 --> 00:21:04,801
Hello. Did you join today?

300
00:21:06,570 --> 00:21:07,838
Let's have a kick-up competition.

301
00:21:08,405 --> 00:21:10,407
One, two…

302
00:21:10,474 --> 00:21:12,309
What're you doing?

303
00:21:12,376 --> 00:21:14,745
What's wrong with you?

304
00:21:14,811 --> 00:21:16,880
I, Riri the Witch,
shall cast a magic spell

305
00:21:16,947 --> 00:21:18,782
to lift your spirits!

306
00:21:22,719 --> 00:21:24,321
It didn't work.

307
00:21:25,021 --> 00:21:26,623
We apologize, please excuse us.

308
00:21:26,690 --> 00:21:27,824
Sorry.

309
00:21:33,663 --> 00:21:34,598
Here you go.

310
00:21:35,098 --> 00:21:36,032
Thanks.

311
00:21:38,502 --> 00:21:40,604
How did the "sharing" go with Ms. Yu?

312
00:21:41,104 --> 00:21:42,572
Thank you for that.

313
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:45,909
I thought I really understood Sora,

314
00:21:47,043 --> 00:21:49,479
but it turns out
there’s still so much I don't know.

315
00:21:50,881 --> 00:21:52,048
I wanted you two

316
00:21:52,115 --> 00:21:55,051
to share your feelings for Sora
with each other

317
00:21:55,118 --> 00:21:57,521
by going through
his photos and his artwork.

318
00:21:59,523 --> 00:22:02,926
First, I wanted you two
to get away from all the pain,

319
00:22:02,993 --> 00:22:05,162
in order to find
even a little bit of peace.

320
00:22:06,997 --> 00:22:07,831
Um…

321
00:22:08,698 --> 00:22:10,801
Why is Sora here?

322
00:22:12,369 --> 00:22:15,138
I ended up bringing him here
a bit forcefully. Sorry.

323
00:22:15,772 --> 00:22:16,606
Not at all.

324
00:22:16,673 --> 00:22:20,243
I hope it helps take his mind off things,
even if only a little.

325
00:22:20,310 --> 00:22:21,478
Yeah.

326
00:22:23,547 --> 00:22:25,849
What is it that Sora likes most right now?

327
00:22:26,650 --> 00:22:29,052
What Sora likes the most right now?

328
00:22:29,119 --> 00:22:31,822
Things like hobbies,
or something he's good at.

329
00:22:42,999 --> 00:22:45,335
I don't know.

330
00:22:46,436 --> 00:22:48,338
It's all right.

331
00:22:52,542 --> 00:22:54,444
Ding dong.

332
00:22:54,511 --> 00:22:56,379
Attention Mr. Tatsuki.

333
00:22:56,446 --> 00:22:57,581
Please gather in the garden.

334
00:22:58,715 --> 00:23:01,051
-Okay.
-Ding dong.

335
00:23:05,055 --> 00:23:06,223
Have fun.

336
00:23:06,289 --> 00:23:07,123
Okay.

337
00:23:09,159 --> 00:23:09,993
What is it?

338
00:23:10,060 --> 00:23:12,229
-Let's go, Tatsuki.
-Let's go.

339
00:23:12,295 --> 00:23:14,331
-Yeah, I'm coming.
-Hurry.

340
00:23:23,273 --> 00:23:25,008
-Want this couch?
-No.

341
00:23:25,075 --> 00:23:26,376
No, sit down.

342
00:23:32,649 --> 00:23:35,151
-Tatsuki!
-This way.

343
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:39,823
Nice! Yeah!

344
00:23:48,231 --> 00:23:50,433
-I did it!
-Congratulations!

345
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:51,701
I did it!

346
00:23:53,436 --> 00:23:55,939
-I'm so glad.
-You did it, Sora.

347
00:24:03,947 --> 00:24:06,016
Hey, can you draw a gorilla?

348
00:24:27,537 --> 00:24:29,406
He's wasting water.

349
00:24:29,472 --> 00:24:31,207
Isn't Tatsuki acting strange?

350
00:24:32,409 --> 00:24:33,743
He's feeling down.

351
00:24:33,810 --> 00:24:36,313
It's like his soul has left his body.

352
00:24:37,414 --> 00:24:39,282
He's forcing himself to smile.

353
00:24:41,184 --> 00:24:44,220
At times like this,
we should cheer him up, huh?

354
00:24:44,287 --> 00:24:46,256
What can we do for him?

355
00:24:49,392 --> 00:24:51,761
I wonder what they're discussing?

356
00:24:55,632 --> 00:24:56,633
Shi-chan?

357
00:24:59,369 --> 00:25:01,738
I wonder what I can do to help.

358
00:25:04,441 --> 00:25:05,976
Yeah, I wonder too.

359
00:25:10,380 --> 00:25:13,416
How about we use the festival
to cheer him up?

360
00:25:14,250 --> 00:25:15,318
Good idea.

361
00:25:15,385 --> 00:25:17,420
But we haven't decided on what to do yet.

362
00:25:18,221 --> 00:25:20,123
He's terrible at sports,

363
00:25:20,190 --> 00:25:21,424
so the baseball tournament is out.

364
00:25:21,491 --> 00:25:22,726
‎Yeah.

365
00:25:22,792 --> 00:25:23,960
No dodgeball either.

366
00:25:24,027 --> 00:25:26,096
-Right.
-He doesn't like yakisoba either.

367
00:25:26,663 --> 00:25:27,497
Really?

368
00:25:27,564 --> 00:25:29,532
Then what should we do?

369
00:25:32,168 --> 00:25:33,003
What about music?

370
00:25:34,871 --> 00:25:37,974
Good idea. Tatsuki will get excited
if we have a music festival.

371
00:25:38,041 --> 00:25:40,310
Sounds good.
We can split up into a few teams,

372
00:25:40,377 --> 00:25:42,045
like for a band or a dance group.

373
00:25:42,112 --> 00:25:42,946
That'll be fun.

374
00:25:43,013 --> 00:25:45,448
All right,
let's go with the music festival.

375
00:25:45,515 --> 00:25:47,617
-Let's do it.
-Yeah.

376
00:25:54,024 --> 00:25:55,225
Tatsuki.

377
00:25:58,662 --> 00:26:00,497
We decided to have a music festival.

378
00:26:01,464 --> 00:26:02,732
I see.

379
00:26:03,333 --> 00:26:04,534
Are you excited?

380
00:26:05,935 --> 00:26:06,903
Yeah. I'm excited.

381
00:26:08,004 --> 00:26:09,439
You don't seem it.

382
00:26:10,540 --> 00:26:11,641
Oh well.

383
00:26:14,644 --> 00:26:15,578
What is it?

384
00:26:18,448 --> 00:26:20,316
The guy that came in today…

385
00:26:23,119 --> 00:26:24,587
Is he your son?

386
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:31,594
How did you know?

387
00:26:33,363 --> 00:26:37,734
Because whenever a new student arrives,
you always go up to them first.

388
00:26:38,868 --> 00:26:40,570
But you didn't do that today.

389
00:26:40,637 --> 00:26:42,038
I see.

390
00:26:45,475 --> 00:26:46,843
Things are still tense?

391
00:26:51,047 --> 00:26:54,684
Well, it won't be easy to mend things.

392
00:26:56,486 --> 00:26:58,588
You should help him the way you helped us.

393
00:27:00,323 --> 00:27:01,891
It's complicated.

394
00:27:04,728 --> 00:27:05,962
Okay,

395
00:27:06,996 --> 00:27:08,465
I guess I'll step in to help out.

396
00:27:09,699 --> 00:27:11,534
No, it's all right.

397
00:27:11,601 --> 00:27:13,336
-Really.
-Don't you worry.

398
00:27:13,937 --> 00:27:15,538
Don't be like that.

399
00:27:16,039 --> 00:27:18,141
Please let me repay the favor.

400
00:27:18,208 --> 00:27:19,476
What's going on?

401
00:27:23,146 --> 00:27:25,215
-Bye Shi-chan.
-Bye.

402
00:27:25,281 --> 00:27:28,051
-Bye.
-See you.

403
00:27:29,219 --> 00:27:30,620
Let's walk back together.

404
00:27:31,955 --> 00:27:33,356
Oh, I forgot something.

405
00:27:33,423 --> 00:27:34,791
You forgot something?

406
00:27:34,858 --> 00:27:36,092
You passed me.

407
00:27:36,159 --> 00:27:37,961
What should I do now?

408
00:27:39,262 --> 00:27:41,865
-Wow. This is very good.
-Yeah.

409
00:27:41,931 --> 00:27:43,500
Sora drew this for me.

410
00:27:44,234 --> 00:27:45,335
Oh, really?

411
00:27:48,938 --> 00:27:50,807
-Bye.
-Bye.

412
00:27:50,874 --> 00:27:51,708
Take care.

413
00:27:51,775 --> 00:27:53,810
-Good.
-It won't move.

414
00:27:54,744 --> 00:27:55,812
Oh no.

415
00:27:56,312 --> 00:27:57,580
I keep falling.

416
00:27:57,647 --> 00:27:58,615
Why?

417
00:28:00,383 --> 00:28:02,118
What's going on?

418
00:28:02,185 --> 00:28:04,287
-You can do it.
-It's okay.

419
00:28:05,555 --> 00:28:06,923
-Soya.
-Yeah?

420
00:28:06,990 --> 00:28:08,057
I'm going to step out.

421
00:28:08,124 --> 00:28:10,059
Oh okay.

422
00:28:11,127 --> 00:28:11,961
FUJINAGA

423
00:28:12,028 --> 00:28:14,230
-A manga?
-Yes.

424
00:28:14,297 --> 00:28:16,933
His drawing was very good, so I wondered

425
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:20,136
if maybe he actually enjoyed
drawing manga?

426
00:28:20,970 --> 00:28:23,506
He used to draw them quite often
until a while ago.

427
00:28:25,008 --> 00:28:27,143
Do you have any of those manga?

428
00:28:28,912 --> 00:28:30,380
I'm not sure.

429
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:33,216
There might be some in his room,

430
00:28:33,283 --> 00:28:35,418
but I'm not sure where it went
after the move.

431
00:28:35,485 --> 00:28:38,655
No problem.
I was just wondering, that's all.

432
00:28:45,061 --> 00:28:47,163
It might be here.

433
00:28:50,300 --> 00:28:52,435
Why do you need his manga?

434
00:28:52,936 --> 00:28:53,870
Oh…

435
00:28:54,370 --> 00:28:56,072
By delving deep into the things

436
00:28:56,139 --> 00:28:59,075
that Sora liked, or was passionate about,

437
00:28:59,142 --> 00:29:01,177
we can sometimes catch a glimpse
of the feelings

438
00:29:01,244 --> 00:29:03,012
hidden deep within his heart.

439
00:29:04,380 --> 00:29:06,716
-Is that right?
-Yes.

440
00:29:15,992 --> 00:29:17,393
What's that…?

441
00:29:19,429 --> 00:29:21,231
He ripped it up himself.

442
00:29:21,865 --> 00:29:25,568
<i>It was around the time</i>
<i>he stopped going to school.</i>

443
00:29:35,979 --> 00:29:38,514
To tear up something that he loved…

444
00:29:41,317 --> 00:29:42,886
He must've been struggling a lot.

445
00:29:47,924 --> 00:29:50,193
But I could do nothing but panic.

446
00:29:50,693 --> 00:29:52,128
I couldn't do anything to help.

447
00:29:54,964 --> 00:29:56,532
I'm so pathetic.

448
00:30:05,508 --> 00:30:07,510
You're not pathetic.

449
00:30:09,979 --> 00:30:12,181
You carefully kept all the things

450
00:30:12,782 --> 00:30:14,117
from his childhood

451
00:30:14,684 --> 00:30:16,786
like his artwork, and his manga.

452
00:30:18,321 --> 00:30:20,523
I can truly feel the love you have

453
00:30:21,391 --> 00:30:22,492
for Sora.

454
00:30:27,196 --> 00:30:31,401
I too, spent my middle
and high school years as a shut-in.

455
00:30:33,136 --> 00:30:35,838
I caused my parents a great deal of worry.

456
00:30:37,674 --> 00:30:40,910
There were times
when I was so anxious and irritable

457
00:30:41,945 --> 00:30:45,014
that I even lashed out and cursed at them.

458
00:30:46,449 --> 00:30:48,851
But my parents
simply watched over me patiently.

459
00:30:50,253 --> 00:30:51,654
And I'm so grateful to them.

460
00:30:54,691 --> 00:30:58,695
I believe that someday
Sora will feel the same way about you.

461
00:30:59,362 --> 00:31:00,830
So

462
00:31:02,532 --> 00:31:04,634
please don't be too harsh on yourself.

463
00:31:12,475 --> 00:31:15,278
It won't do any good
if I can't stay strong.

464
00:31:19,983 --> 00:31:20,950
Um…

465
00:31:21,617 --> 00:31:24,988
May I borrow that?

466
00:31:29,258 --> 00:31:30,093
Yes.

467
00:31:49,746 --> 00:31:50,713
You're awake?

468
00:31:56,219 --> 00:31:57,420
Do you know <i>Brave Drop</i>?

469
00:31:58,788 --> 00:31:59,889
Have you ever played it?

470
00:32:01,491 --> 00:32:02,325
Yeah.

471
00:32:02,392 --> 00:32:05,194
Really? Can you help me out?

472
00:32:21,978 --> 00:32:22,979
What's your name?

473
00:32:25,481 --> 00:32:26,349
Sora.

474
00:32:29,018 --> 00:32:30,353
I'm Tomoki.

475
00:32:34,524 --> 00:32:36,893
-Hey Shi-chan.
-I'm back.

476
00:32:47,003 --> 00:32:47,904
Mr. Tatsuki.

477
00:32:49,839 --> 00:32:51,541
Do you have a minute?

478
00:33:01,617 --> 00:33:03,252
What's this?

479
00:33:03,319 --> 00:33:05,721
It's Sora's manga notebook.

480
00:33:08,257 --> 00:33:10,193
When he was in middle school,

481
00:33:10,259 --> 00:33:12,495
around the time
when he stopped going to school,

482
00:33:13,162 --> 00:33:15,198
he apparently tore it up himself.

483
00:33:39,388 --> 00:33:41,991
I never knew he had been drawing so much.

484
00:33:43,259 --> 00:33:46,662
Right now, the pages
are all scattered and unreadable…

485
00:33:48,431 --> 00:33:50,199
but why don't we try
piecing them back together?

486
00:33:52,802 --> 00:33:55,238
I was just wondering if, perhaps,

487
00:33:55,805 --> 00:33:57,206
Sora's bottled-up feelings

488
00:33:57,273 --> 00:33:59,842
might be hidden somewhere
within this manga.

489
00:34:01,010 --> 00:34:02,712
It's just a thought.

490
00:34:10,253 --> 00:34:11,087
I'll give it a try.

491
00:34:12,288 --> 00:34:13,523
I'll help out too.

492
00:34:14,857 --> 00:34:16,225
I may not look it,

493
00:34:16,292 --> 00:34:18,194
but I'm actually pretty good
at jigsaw puzzles.

494
00:34:26,903 --> 00:34:28,171
What do you think

495
00:34:30,673 --> 00:34:31,841
about Tatsuki?

496
00:34:38,781 --> 00:34:39,715
Nothing really…

497
00:34:41,384 --> 00:34:42,418
Nothing in particular.

498
00:34:45,922 --> 00:34:47,056
I see.

499
00:34:49,192 --> 00:34:50,493
It doesn't matter anyway.

500
00:34:53,930 --> 00:34:54,964
I see.

501
00:34:58,334 --> 00:34:59,902
Maybe it's because he's your dad.

502
00:35:02,838 --> 00:35:03,773
What do you mean?

503
00:35:06,642 --> 00:35:08,444
Everyone here

504
00:35:10,012 --> 00:35:11,714
loves Tatsuki.

505
00:35:15,685 --> 00:35:16,786
Why?

506
00:35:18,387 --> 00:35:19,455
How should I put it…?

507
00:35:23,292 --> 00:35:26,362
We're pretty messed up,

508
00:35:29,031 --> 00:35:31,033
but he accepts everything about us.

509
00:35:32,702 --> 00:35:34,637
And he always has our backs.

510
00:35:35,771 --> 00:35:36,806
Are you sure

511
00:35:38,140 --> 00:35:39,475
you're not being fooled?

512
00:35:41,978 --> 00:35:43,613
He's not really that nice of a guy.

513
00:35:45,715 --> 00:35:46,716
Is that right?

514
00:35:52,388 --> 00:35:53,356
It's over.

515
00:35:57,526 --> 00:35:58,694
You can still keep going.

516
00:35:59,328 --> 00:36:01,097
There's a shortcut ahead.

517
00:36:14,510 --> 00:36:16,345
You weren't talking about the game?

518
00:36:18,247 --> 00:36:19,315
It's nothing.

519
00:36:31,460 --> 00:36:32,662
Sora,

520
00:36:35,631 --> 00:36:37,133
I think we're alike.

521
00:36:39,035 --> 00:36:39,969
‎What?

522
00:36:43,072 --> 00:36:43,939
Back when

523
00:36:46,108 --> 00:36:48,577
I was in my second year of middle school,
I got bullied.

524
00:36:51,781 --> 00:36:53,683
I stopped going to school

525
00:36:57,286 --> 00:36:59,422
and just spent all day in my room
playing video games.

526
00:37:02,725 --> 00:37:06,295
I couldn't understand my studies at all,

527
00:37:08,331 --> 00:37:10,366
and everyone around me
was talking about entrance exams…

528
00:37:14,003 --> 00:37:15,037
but I didn't feel like

529
00:37:17,039 --> 00:37:19,008
I was capable of going anywhere.

530
00:37:28,684 --> 00:37:32,488
I thought, "My life is completely over."

531
00:37:35,825 --> 00:37:37,560
And I intended to kill myself.

532
00:37:42,331 --> 00:37:43,299
I was serious.

533
00:37:45,835 --> 00:37:46,802
I'm

534
00:37:49,105 --> 00:37:50,206
going to end my life here.

535
00:37:52,041 --> 00:37:53,709
-What?
<i>-But…</i>

536
00:37:54,877 --> 00:37:56,912
Tatsuki came to stop me.

537
00:38:00,216 --> 00:38:02,518
He told me not to end my life.

538
00:38:04,220 --> 00:38:05,554
He was so persistent.

539
00:38:11,861 --> 00:38:13,829
He said his son
tried to take his own life too…

540
00:38:16,532 --> 00:38:17,433
So

541
00:38:18,501 --> 00:38:21,604
he would never repeat
the same mistake again.

542
00:38:24,940 --> 00:38:26,909
Even after hearing that,

543
00:38:30,112 --> 00:38:31,680
I was serious about my decision.

544
00:38:34,917 --> 00:38:36,585
-Bye.
-Tomoki!

545
00:38:37,153 --> 00:38:38,187
<i>Then…</i>

546
00:38:38,921 --> 00:38:40,756
<i>while trying to save me,</i>

547
00:38:42,024 --> 00:38:43,826
<i>he fell down instead.</i>

548
00:38:47,596 --> 00:38:48,731
What?

549
00:38:50,266 --> 00:38:51,767
You normally couldn't

550
00:38:53,769 --> 00:38:55,704
do something like that, could you?

551
00:38:58,707 --> 00:39:00,810
Even though he was the one
who almost died,

552
00:39:01,944 --> 00:39:03,979
he was still worrying about me.

553
00:39:05,448 --> 00:39:06,749
Tomoki.

554
00:39:07,850 --> 00:39:09,185
I'm so glad

555
00:39:10,319 --> 00:39:11,487
you're alive.

556
00:39:13,722 --> 00:39:16,358
I was like, what's wrong with this guy?

557
00:39:29,472 --> 00:39:30,639
Tatsuki

558
00:39:33,142 --> 00:39:34,643
is amazing.

559
00:39:41,884 --> 00:39:42,952
That can't be true.

560
00:39:48,424 --> 00:39:49,725
You can't believe it?

561
00:39:53,229 --> 00:39:55,364
He's not that kind of a guy at all.

562
00:40:01,270 --> 00:40:02,137
I see.

563
00:40:11,080 --> 00:40:13,449
I think this is the last one.

564
00:40:29,732 --> 00:40:31,500
We pieced it all together.

565
00:40:34,703 --> 00:40:36,505
I'll be going home now.

566
00:40:39,408 --> 00:40:40,342
Thank you.

567
00:40:58,193 --> 00:40:59,495
Should we call it a day?

568
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:05,901
Okay.

569
00:41:12,341 --> 00:41:15,444
It's all right. I'll do the rest.

570
00:41:18,414 --> 00:41:19,448
Sora,

571
00:41:20,749 --> 00:41:22,318
you have something else to do, right?

572
00:41:40,603 --> 00:41:41,770
SEASHELL

573
00:41:41,837 --> 00:41:43,105
IT'S A PRETTY SEASHELL

574
00:41:43,172 --> 00:41:44,440
WHAT A BEAUTIFUL SOUND

575
00:41:47,176 --> 00:41:48,444
Here, this is for you.

576
00:41:48,510 --> 00:41:49,878
It's pretty.

577
00:41:49,945 --> 00:41:51,547
Okay, Dad, let's race.

578
00:42:11,967 --> 00:42:12,901
This

579
00:42:13,936 --> 00:42:15,070
is nice.

580
00:42:17,973 --> 00:42:18,941
You

581
00:42:20,175 --> 00:42:21,377
liked drawing manga?

582
00:42:27,683 --> 00:42:30,352
I never knew you had put in so much effort

583
00:42:31,520 --> 00:42:32,988
drawing manga like this.

584
00:42:39,662 --> 00:42:41,230
Sora, it's okay

585
00:42:42,064 --> 00:42:43,332
for you to do whatever

586
00:42:44,633 --> 00:42:45,701
you want to do.

587
00:42:51,206 --> 00:42:53,542
You're saying that for real?

588
00:42:55,310 --> 00:42:58,047
What if I end up
turning into a good-for-nothing adult?

589
00:43:00,149 --> 00:43:01,450
Who you are right now is what--

590
00:43:01,517 --> 00:43:03,085
That's just lip service.

591
00:43:04,687 --> 00:43:05,621
Deep down,

592
00:43:06,722 --> 00:43:08,490
you really think I'm no good,

593
00:43:08,557 --> 00:43:09,391
don't you?

594
00:43:09,458 --> 00:43:10,893
No, never.

595
00:43:13,662 --> 00:43:15,064
Everyone's fawning over you

596
00:43:15,631 --> 00:43:17,066
yelling, "Tatsuki! Tatsuki!"

597
00:43:17,666 --> 00:43:18,734
So you're smiling like a fool

598
00:43:20,269 --> 00:43:21,637
letting it all go to your head.

599
00:43:23,505 --> 00:43:24,840
Even with Tomoki…

600
00:43:26,775 --> 00:43:28,477
You risked your life to save him, right?

601
00:43:32,948 --> 00:43:33,916
Why…

602
00:43:35,384 --> 00:43:36,218
Why…

603
00:43:36,719 --> 00:43:38,287
Why do you risk your life

604
00:43:39,154 --> 00:43:40,956
to save others

605
00:43:42,524 --> 00:43:43,459
while I…

606
00:43:48,997 --> 00:43:50,899
While I've ended up like this…?

607
00:43:57,639 --> 00:43:59,241
-Why?
-Sora.

608
00:44:01,844 --> 00:44:05,714
You're acting like such a good guy
when you're actually a jerk.

609
00:44:06,448 --> 00:44:08,150
Stop putting up a front!

610
00:44:11,153 --> 00:44:13,722
Stop staring in silence and say something!

611
00:44:16,959 --> 00:44:18,060
Which one…

612
00:44:19,728 --> 00:44:20,929
Which one…

613
00:44:22,064 --> 00:44:24,566
Which one is the real you?

614
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:38,947
PREVIEW OF THE NEXT EPISODE

615
00:44:39,014 --> 00:44:41,049
THIS DRAMA IS FICTIONAL

616
00:44:41,116 --> 00:44:42,050
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita

